## LOOM ORCHESTRATION REFERENCE

**Session start:** read your Knowledge Brief, find your session ID in `.loom/work/signals/`, scan for `EXECUTION PLAN` blocks, spawn per Rule 6; else ask the user.

**Stage lifecycle:** `WaitingForDeps → Queued → Executing → Completed → Verified` (also `Blocked`, `NeedsHandoff`, `WaitingForInput`). Retry a failed merge: `loom stage merge <stage-id>`.

**CLI:** `loom run` | `loom status` | `loom stop` | `loom check <stage-id> [--suggest]` | `loom knowledge sync` | `loom repair [--fix]`.

**Handoff** (`.loom/work/handoffs/YYYY-MM-DD-desc.md`, written by `loom handoff` per Rule 3): `# Handoff: [Description]`, `**Stage**: [id]`, `## Completed` with file:line refs, `## Next Steps` prioritized.

**References:** cite code as `src/auth.ts:45-120`, not "the auth file".

